    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Identity key redesign** (`Owner.getIdentityKey()` in `model/Owner.java`)\n- Was: plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`.\n- Now: lower-case SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` \u2014 a 64-char `[0-9a-f]` string. The household id is no longer part of identity.\n\n**New `model/Soundex.java`** \u2014 standard American Soundex encoder (first letter + three digits, vowels separate, H/W don't), used by both the identity key and the soft-match.\n\n**`model/Sha256.java`** \u2014 added `lowerHex(...)` alongside the existing upper-case `hex(...)`, since the identity key needs lower-case hex while the customer code / household id keep upper-case.\n\n**409 duplicate detection** (`EnsureUniqueIdentity`) \u2014 logic unchanged and still correct: candidates are narrowed by `findByTelephone` (valid because the telephone is a component of the hashed input, so equal keys require equal telephones), deleted owners ignored, exact key match \u2192 409. Only the Javadoc was updated. The email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in the pipeline (`RejectDisposableEmail`), unchanged.\n\n**Soft-match** (`DetectPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 rewritten to the new rule: flag when an existing non-deleted owner has a **different identity key** but a **matching soundex(lastName)** and **identical postcode**. This makes two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones a soft match (not a 409), as specified. Declared household members and owners without a postcode are still never flagged.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated Javadocs on `AssignHouseholdId`, `DuplicateIdentityException`, the `possibleDuplicateOf` field, and the `identityKey`/`possibleDuplicate` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to match the new behaviour.\n\n## Verification\n- `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` \u2014 identity key is now 64-char lowercase hex \u2713\n- `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 identical telephone/email/lastName still 409 \u2713\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: the soft-match now scans `findByLastName`'s replacement `findAll()` rather than a prefixed last-name query, because soundex must catch spelling variants (\"Smith\"/\"Smyth\") that a last-name-prefix query would miss \u2014 there's no soundex or postcode index on the repository to narrow further.",
